  "scope": "A declared finite carrier mechanism couples active maintenance to the unchanged physical clock during absent sensing. Equilibrium and sensory loss are distinct inputs and protocols. A charged two-unit physical reserve extends the complete body to 24 states. One missing-sensing tick at any start preserves every-time Exchange score one. Three or more consecutive missing-sensing ticks empty every supported body from the third tick onward. The original full-state marginal-ghost cut retains a quarter gap from tick seven. Twenty-four fixed material identities realize both normal/cut and arbitrary protocols with eight accessible source units, exact score transport and explicit recharging; initial body-plus-source energy is twelve. This does not assert a uniform per-tick law for all carriers, an exact two-tick functional boundary, new complete encoding, physical thermodynamic calibration, or the full L1-L6 goal.",
